---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SectionRule from "../components/SectionRule.astro";
---

<Base title="About" active="About">
  <main class="pagehead">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1 class="display">How a keyboard<br />becomes a signature.</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-l">
      <SectionRule label="Overview" />
      <p>
        <b>KOTTU</b> is a behavioral authentication system. It verifies a person’s
        identity from their unique typing patterns rather than relying on the
        password alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        It analyses keystroke dynamics — how long each key is held, and the
        timing between consecutive keystrokes — across a fixed passphrase. A
        recurrent neural network reads those rhythms and recognises the typist.
      </p>

      <SectionRule label="Why it holds up" />
      <p>
        Traditional authentication checks <b>what a person knows</b>: a password
        or PIN. KOTTU adds a check on <b>how they type</b> it. Typing rhythm is
        specific to an individual and difficult to reproduce, so an attacker who
        knows the password still can’t reproduce the cadence behind it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same signal extends to continuous authentication — verifying a person
        throughout a session, not only at login.
      </p>

      <SectionRule label="How it works" />
      <div class="grid2">
        <div>
          <h3>Data</h3>
          <p>
            CMU DSL-StrongPasswordData: 51 subjects, each typing
            <code>.tie5Roanl</code> 400 times. 31 timing features per attempt —
            hold times and down-down / up-down gaps.
          </p>
          <h3>Model</h3>
          <p>
            Each attempt is reshaped into an 11-step sequence and read by a
            two-layer LSTM with dropout, ending in a 51-way softmax over the
            enrolled identities.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Training</h3>
          <p>
            Stratified 64 / 16 / 20 split, standardised features, up to 30 epochs
            with early stopping on validation loss.
          </p>
          <h3>Evaluation</h3>
          <p>
            Weighted accuracy, precision, recall and F1 on a 4,080-sample
            held-out set, plus a per-class report and confusion matrix.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <SectionRule label="Next" />
      <ul>
        <li>Wire the trained model into the Authenticate screen for live scoring</li>
        <li>Export raw training history and the confusion matrix for native charts</li>
        <li>Continuous, session-long authentication</li>
        <li>Larger rosters and stronger sequence models</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="muted mt-l">KOTTU v1.0 · Behavioral Authentication System</p>
  </main>
</Base>
